1
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:29,800
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,480
Y 'all move!

3
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:02,770
Hurry up!

4
00:01:02,853 --> 00:01:04,017
The duel's about to start!

5
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:06,865
It's being broadcast live
all around the world!

6
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:09,269
Remember our deal, Devlin.

7
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:11,320
I win this and you let Joey go.

8
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:13,600
No more dog suit, no more demands.

9
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:15,050
Agreed.

10
00:01:15,133 --> 00:01:17,677
Just don't forget the
flip side to that coin.

11
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:22,320
You lose this game, and you promise to
never play Duel Monsters ever again.

12
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:24,570
Now!

13
00:01:24,653 --> 00:01:25,940
Let's get it on!

14
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:31,364
Looks a bit different
than a dueling arena, huh?

15
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:33,095
Well, get used to it.

16
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:37,197
Dungeon Dice Monsters is a whole new
game with a whole new set of rules.

17
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:40,809
And to keep up, you're going
to have to pay close attention.

18
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:42,641
Don't you worry.

19
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:44,020
I'm a quick study.

20
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:47,937
You better be, Yugi, because I
know this game inside and out.

21
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:50,957
And if you want to win, you're
going to have to learn it as well.

22
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:52,460
Now let's get started.

23
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:56,667
Looks pretty straightforward

24
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:00,760
Lost already? Relax,

25
00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:05,097
I'll walk you through it That's
your dice pool Select 15 dice from

26
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:09,100
it to use for the game I'd give
you some tips on which to pick,

27
00:02:09,260 --> 00:02:13,672
Yugi But being the master gamer that
you are, I'm sure you'll figure it out

28
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:19,342
With all these different colors and designs,
it's hard to know which ones to choose

29
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:23,200
Hurry up now I got mine already set.

30
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:25,180
I'm ready too. Good.

31
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:26,917
Now here's how it works.

32
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,897
These dice are gonna be
kinda like your dueling deck.

33
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:33,840
And just like you shuffle your
deck, we shuffle these. Like this.

34
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:37,760
See? Easy.

35
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:42,100
The Dice Automator will randomize
your 15 dice in groups of three.

36
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:43,440
Take a look.

37
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,660
You get three dice per round.

38
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:47,677
You roll all three at the same time,

39
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:50,557
and then you get to make your
move depending on what you roll.

40
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:53,287
But I'll explain more
about that a bit later.

41
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:56,906
Now, take the three die
out of the auto hatch.

42
00:02:59,140 --> 00:02:59,970
Okay.

43
00:03:00,053 --> 00:03:01,334
Now, how do you score?

44
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:04,080
Well, in this game, we have heart points.

45
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:06,837
They're like life points,
only you only get three.

46
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:07,750
That's it.

47
00:03:07,833 --> 00:03:10,953
And whoever loses all three
of their hearts first is out.

48
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,160
Game on!

49
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:13,960
What game on?

50
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:15,817
But Yuki just now learned the rules.

51
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:18,547
Yeah, that's probably
just how Duke likes it.

52
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:20,557
Go! Go! Go!

53
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:21,860
Go, dude, go!

54
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:23,800
Thanks, ladies.

55
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:25,020
You're beautiful.

56
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:26,720
Hooray! Hooray!

57
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:29,660
Man, what a bunch of suck-ups.

58
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:31,540
No yapping, you mutt!

59
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:34,220
This is a duel, not a dog show!

60
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:40,320
I'm gonna make my first roll now, Yugi,

61
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:45,297
so from here on out you're just gonna have
to listen carefully and learn as we go.

62
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:46,851
See those markings there?

63
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:48,637
Those are called crests.

64
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:50,837
Different crests do different things.

65
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:52,880
Take that green die, for example.

66
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:56,540
That star crest I just
rolled is for summoning.

67
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:58,717
To be able to summon something,

68
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:01,317
at least two out of the three
dice that you roll during your

69
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:04,900
turn have to land with the
same type summon crest face-up.

70
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,940
And if I'm not mistaken,

71
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:09,257
it seems I've come up with
two matching summoning

72
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:11,800
crests on my very first roll of the game.

73
00:04:12,140 --> 00:04:14,900
Now, the dimensionalizing
part of the process.

74
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:16,660
Dimension the dice!

75
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:22,500
And there you go! Ryukashin!

76
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:25,220
My very first monster is on the board!

77
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:27,721
The monsters are inside the dice?

78
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:29,040
And that's not all!

79
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:32,057
It looks like the dice
themselves are part of the game!

80
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:35,437
I'm glad that you made that point,
my little cheerleader-in-waiting.

81
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:39,640
That's one of the key elements to
Dungeon Dice Monsters. For you see,

82
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:44,217
once a die unfolds to dimensionalize a
monster, it becomes a dungeon pathway.

83
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:47,577
And with enough of this dungeon
pathway, I can construct a route.

84
00:04:47,660 --> 00:04:52,300
a route my monsters can use to get
to your heart points. Oh, I get it.

85
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:55,097
The way to destroy your
opponent's heart points is to get

86
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:58,257
your monsters close enough to
attack the hearts directly.

87
00:04:58,340 --> 00:05:03,137
So, the more dice that I can dimensionalize
and turn into Dungeon Path, the better.

88
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:04,455
Sounds simple enough.

89
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:07,780
Go ahead, Yugi.

90
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,100
It's your turn.

91
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:11,740
Devlin, don't you forget.

92
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:16,017
If I win this, then you have to give
my friend Joey his freedom back.

93
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:17,340
Right, if you win.

94
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:20,108
I'm counting on you, buddy.

95
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:22,817
If there's anyone that can
beat this guy Devlin, it's you.

96
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:24,440
No talking, bad dog.

97
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:26,860
We're with you, Yugi.

98
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:28,980
Yeah, all the way, buddy.

99
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:31,440
Long live the king of games.

100
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,860
His reign is over.

101
00:05:34,180 --> 00:05:36,240
Today, this cheat is going down.

102
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:38,900
Go, dice roll.

103
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:43,256
The three crests, none of them match.

104
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:46,857
Yeah, because the level of dice
you threw were way too high.

105
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:50,800
Sorry, didn't I mention that
different dice had different levels?

106
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,160
This is how it works.

107
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:56,909
There are six types of crests
on the surfaces of these dice.

108
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,412
Summon, movement, magic, attack,
defense, and trap crests.

109
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:07,397
How often each of these crests appears
on a dice depends on that dice's level.

110
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:11,457
The level two dice that I just used
had three summon crests on each,

111
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:13,637
so it was easy for me to roll two of them.

112
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:17,900
But the easier a monster is
to summon, the weaker he is.

113
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:21,240
Okay, now look carefully
at your dice, Yugi.

114
00:06:23,260 --> 00:06:25,900
They each have only one summon crest.

115
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:30,991
Right, and that makes it much more
difficult for you to roll a pair of them.

116
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:34,433
Of course, had you, it'd have
been a very strong monster.

117
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:38,197
Still, I'm of the opinion that
in the early stages of the game,

118
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:40,257
it's better to go for
a low-level sure thing.

119
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:45,105
After all, the odds of summoning a monster
with high-level dice are slim to none.

120
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:46,340
Oh, no.

121
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:49,367
Almost all the dice I
picked were high-level.

122
00:06:56,020 --> 00:07:00,117
Sorry, Yugi, but if all you have are
high-level dice at your disposal,

123
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:03,637
you're going to have a real hard
time summoning any monsters.

124
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:05,460
I can't believe this.

125
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:09,960
The game just started, and I'm
already at a huge disadvantage.

126
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:12,580
Hey, this ain't fair, Duke.

127
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:15,977
You should have told Yugi all the
rules before the game started.

128
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:18,877
This different dice level
stuff changes everything.

129
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:20,677
You should start the game fresh.

130
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:22,720
If it were someone else, maybe.

131
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:25,680
But not the king of games. He'll be okay.

132
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,740
Go, dice roll!

133
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:34,450
Yes!

134
00:07:34,533 --> 00:07:36,137
Another two summoning crests.

135
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:40,660
My dungeon path will extend, and now
I'll have two monsters on the field.

136
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:45,300
Dimension the dice and unlock Duranto!

137
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:54,197
His dungeon path is getting closer
and closer to my heart points,

138
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:56,257
and I'm not even on the board yet.

139
00:07:56,340 --> 00:07:57,811
I'm coming for you, Yugi.

140
00:07:58,020 --> 00:08:00,617
And since I just rolled
a movement crest too,

141
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:05,053
I can use it to advance my monster
even further along the dungeon pathway.

142
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,120
Oh, FYI, if you don't want
to use a crest you rolled,

143
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:11,957
you can save them for
later in your crest pool.

144
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,120
Now go ahead.

145
00:08:13,380 --> 00:08:14,300
It's your turn.

146
00:08:14,980 --> 00:08:16,360
Go, dice roll!

147
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:20,380
Still no matching crests.

148
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:22,620
Ha-ha, nothing again, huh?

149
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:26,158
Maybe you ought to try
blowing on them for good luck.

150
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:27,540
My turn now.

151
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:29,580
Go, dice roll!

152
00:08:32,660 --> 00:08:34,357
Well, would you look at that?

153
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:36,100
It's another summoning.

154
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:39,460
And look at the surprise inside.

155
00:08:40,300 --> 00:08:41,460
Gator dragon.

156
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:45,400
And I'll use the movement
crest I rolled to advance him.

157
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:47,740
My roll now.

158
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:51,440
At last, two summoning crests.

159
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:53,160
I can play a monster.

160
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:55,000
No, you can't.

161
00:08:55,140 --> 00:08:58,477
You've rolled two summoning crests,
but their levels aren't the same.

162
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:00,577
It doesn't count. I thought...

163
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:01,997
It's my turn again.

164
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,620
Ooh, level four dice.

165
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,937
They were too hot for you to handle.

166
00:09:07,020 --> 00:09:08,700
But let's see how I can do.

167
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:10,580
Go, dice roll!

168
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:15,040
Oh, what can I say?

169
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:19,677
I guess Lady Luck has got the hots for
old Duke Devlin, like everyone else.

170
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:20,995
I mean, what is that?

171
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:23,400
Four summonings in a row?

172
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:28,680
A chest?

173
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:34,300
This is an item summoning Yugi, But
more on that a bit later. Now roll.

174
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:39,860
No, another miss. You know,

175
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:43,817
maybe we should change your title from
the King of Games to the King of Lame.

176
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:47,677
I mean, at this rate, I'll have you
beat even before you're on the board.

177
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:52,120
I knew that you weren't the
real deal, Yu-Gi. Go! Dice roll!

178
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:54,650
Yes!

179
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:55,797
Another summoning.

180
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:58,657
Now I'll have a monster
right by your heart points.

181
00:09:58,740 --> 00:09:59,940
Dimension the dice!

182
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:03,420
Check it out!

183
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:05,220
The 13th Grave!

184
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:12,440
That 13th Grave is just three squares
away from being able to attack me.

185
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:15,348
I have to summon a
monster and take him out.

186
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:18,068
Otherwise, I'll lose a
heart point for sure.

187
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,800
Come on! Let's go!

188
00:10:19,940 --> 00:10:21,352
Our audience is waiting.

189
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:24,717
And soon, they're going to see
you for what you really are.

190
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:27,920
A loser who could have
never truly beaten Pegasus.

191
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:29,310
This is it.

192
00:10:29,393 --> 00:10:32,317
No matter how high the odds
are stacked against me,

193
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:35,857
I have to believe it's possible
to roll two Summon Crests here.

194
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:40,060
The same way I believed in the
heart of the cards. Go! Dice roll!

195
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:46,830
Ha!

196
00:10:46,913 --> 00:10:47,820
Not a Summon Crest!

197
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,100
I got one.

198
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,200
Now if only...

199
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:59,840
There, I rolled two
level four Summon Crests.

200
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:04,480
Now I can finally summon a monster
and defend my heart points.

201
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:06,180
Dimension the Dice!

202
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,840
The Mighty Mage!

203
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:15,480
And next,

204
00:11:15,620 --> 00:11:19,977
I'll access my Crest Pool Dice and
use a movement crest to move my mage

205
00:11:20,060 --> 00:11:24,140
one space forward so he can launch
an attack against the 13th grade.

206
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:25,780
Lightning step!

207
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:31,320
All right! In your face! Yes!

208
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,737
Knowing this game and all
of its rules may have given

209
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:38,617
you the advantage in assembling
your creatures against me,

210
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:41,560
but now I have a monster of my own.

211
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:49,740
Did you see Yugi's last move?

212
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:52,170
Incredible!

213
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:54,497
He busted out that level four monster like

214
00:11:54,580 --> 00:11:57,168
he's played dungeon
dice monsters for years!

215
00:11:59,080 --> 00:11:59,910
You!

216
00:11:59,993 --> 00:12:00,823
Keep it up, buddy!

217
00:12:00,906 --> 00:12:02,197
You're really doing great!

218
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:03,457
What do you think, Taya?

219
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:04,997
Is Yugi in the clear now?

220
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:06,700
No, I don't think so.

221
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:10,057
Duke's dungeon path is way
more widespread than Yugi's,

222
00:12:10,140 --> 00:12:12,677
and he's still got more
monsters out on the board, too.

223
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:15,289
Yugi has a long way to
go to win this game.

224
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,357
Congratulations on your
first monster, Yugi.

225
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:22,297
Just four more now, and
you'll have as many as I do.

226
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:25,260
My turn now. Go! Dice roll!

227
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:28,550
Whoops.

228
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:29,580
Spoke too soon.

229
00:12:29,740 --> 00:12:30,916
Make that five more.

230
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:33,840
Dimension the dice!

231
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:39,700
I've unlocked the Blast Lizard!

232
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:44,321
But don't be fooled by his
low-level status, Yugi.

233
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:46,177
When played in just the right way,

234
00:12:46,260 --> 00:12:50,360
Last Lizard has a special attack
that packs a surprising punch.

235
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:51,940
Special attack?

236
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:55,597
Sounds like another rule that Duke
conveniently forgot to mention.

237
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:57,327
I'll have to be on my guard.

238
00:12:57,460 --> 00:12:58,660
My roll now.

239
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:00,230
Oh, cool.

240
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:01,656
Some low-level dice.

241
00:13:01,820 --> 00:13:03,857
I knew I had at least a few of these.

242
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:05,857
It should be easier to summon now.

243
00:13:05,940 --> 00:13:07,180
Go, dice roll!

244
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:10,280
All right, two crests.

245
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:12,220
Dimension the dice!

246
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:19,920
The Winged Dragon,
Guardian of the Fortress.

247
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:23,632
Now you have two monsters of
mine to contend with, Devlin.

248
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,940
Not for long, Yugi.

249
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:27,220
It's my turn.

250
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:28,740
Go, dice roll!

251
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:33,140
You failed to summon anything.

252
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:37,851
Whoever said I was trying to
summon a monster on this roll?

253
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:39,290
What?

254
00:13:39,373 --> 00:13:40,500
Boy, are you dense.

255
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:44,657
Remember what I said about playing my
blast lizard in just the right way?

256
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:47,597
So then, you were rolling
for his special attack?

257
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:49,097
That's kinda right, Yugi.

258
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:52,737
The Blast Lizard's special attack
requires four Magic Crests.

259
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:57,277
I already had two in my Crest pool, so
I needed to roll two more, which I did.

260
00:13:57,360 --> 00:14:01,440
So now, I'll use a Movement Crest
to position my Blast Lizard.

261
00:14:01,580 --> 00:14:05,200
And next, use my four Magic
Crests to have him attack you!

262
00:14:13,940 --> 00:14:15,020
That's too bad.

263
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:18,440
You worked so hard to summon
that winged dragon, too.

264
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:20,110
Yay!

265
00:14:20,193 --> 00:14:21,240
We love you, Dookie-Pow!

266
00:14:22,340 --> 00:14:23,380
Don't give up.

267
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:24,980
You can beat him, Yugi.

268
00:14:25,380 --> 00:14:26,400
It's my turn.

269
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:27,740
Go, dice roll!

270
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:32,460
Not one summoning crest
died. It's my turn.

271
00:14:32,700 --> 00:14:33,660
Go, dice roll!

272
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:37,457
Look, another summoning.

273
00:14:37,540 --> 00:14:39,540
And with level three dice as well.

274
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:41,940
Dimension the dice!

275
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:45,980
Dark assailant!

276
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:52,360
And now I'll dip into my crest pool
again and close in on your heart points.

277
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:54,597
By using two movement crests,

278
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:59,420
I put Blast Lizard and Gator Dragon
within striking distance of your hearts.

279
00:15:00,020 --> 00:15:01,780
Go ahead, take your turn.

280
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:05,431
Nothing you roll is going to
help you get out of this mess.

281
00:15:05,820 --> 00:15:09,477
I mean, I don't even think that I'd
be able to find a way to pull it off,

282
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:11,795
and I'm the one who invented the game.

283
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:13,320
You're its inventor?

284
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:15,317
I knew you were its champion, but...

285
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:19,140
I'm both, and everyone in the
entire world should know it!

286
00:15:19,980 --> 00:15:20,810
What?

287
00:15:20,893 --> 00:15:24,917
I should be known as the second greatest
game creator in all of the world by now,

288
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:25,830
Yugi,

289
00:15:25,913 --> 00:15:29,040
but I'm not, and it's all
because of your cheating ways.

290
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:33,017
That's the only way you could have
beaten a great man like Pegasus.

291
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:34,657
He has twice the skills you have.

292
00:15:34,740 --> 00:15:37,420
You ruined my life on that day, Yu-Gi.

293
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:42,220
The defeat that you handed Pegasus
changed everything for me. But how?

294
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:47,080
I dedicated my life to
creating Dungeon Dice Monsters.

295
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:52,240
I spent all of my free time perfecting
its gameplay and fine-tuning its rules.

296
00:15:52,580 --> 00:15:57,217
And when I was finished, it was clear that
I had created something truly remarkable.

297
00:15:57,300 --> 00:16:02,400
I decided I had to send it to the only
man who could possibly appreciate it,

298
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:03,430
Pegasus.

299
00:16:03,513 --> 00:16:04,760
A couple of days passed,

300
00:16:04,860 --> 00:16:06,377
but I didn't hear anything from that great

301
00:16:06,460 --> 00:16:10,140
game master until I got this crazy e-mail.

302
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:12,380
He said he'd read my proposal.

303
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:15,400
I couldn't believe my eyes.

304
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:17,800
E-mail for Devlin Boy.

305
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:19,320
E-mail for Devlin Boy.

306
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:22,077
He said he wanted to fly
me out on his personal

307
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:24,937
helicopter so that we could
discuss the game in person.

308
00:16:25,020 --> 00:16:25,850
Yeah!

309
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:31,300
The very next day, I was
brought to Pegasus' island,

310
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:32,961
Duelist Kingdom.

311
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:34,672
I can hardly believe it.

312
00:16:34,900 --> 00:16:37,160
All my hard work was paying off.

313
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:42,920
I was going to meet my
idol, Maximilian Pegasus.

314
00:16:43,660 --> 00:16:48,580
When we met, Pegasus immediately challenged
me to a game of dungeon dice monsters.

315
00:16:49,020 --> 00:16:52,240
I expected him to be good,
but he was phenomenal.

316
00:16:52,620 --> 00:16:56,657
It was his first time playing the
game, and he completely overpowered me.

317
00:16:56,740 --> 00:16:58,740
Me, the guy who created it.

318
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:00,620
I was amazed with his skills.

319
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:03,840
Looks like I win.

320
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:05,900
Whoa, you're good.

321
00:17:06,660 --> 00:17:11,600
Well, Devlin boy, I must say this Dungeon
Dice Monsters game is really something.

322
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:13,900
I thoroughly enjoyed it.

323
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:19,460
And together, we'll see to it that the
whole world does as well. Partners?

324
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:21,980
Oh, I'd be honored, Mr. Pegasus.

325
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:25,100
And with that, the deal was sealed.

326
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:31,897
He told me we'd draw off the official
contract After he finished hosting a dueling

327
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:34,237
tournament That was about
to take place on his

328
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:37,400
island The tournament
that you were headed to,

329
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:42,820
Yugi And ever since you beat him there I
haven't been able to contact him at all

330
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:49,797
Everything that I'd worked for was
shattered that day And it's all your

331
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:55,040
fault You don't know what kind of man
Pegasus was at all He was a great man,

332
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:59,820
until you came along and broke his
spirit with your dirty, cheating ways.

333
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,880
And now I'll get my
revenge by breaking you.

334
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:14,700
Now, Yu-Gi, I'll expose you for what you
really are, a good-for-nothing cheater.

335
00:18:15,060 --> 00:18:18,760
I've never cheated at anything
in my entire life. Please,

336
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:21,577
you expect me to believe
that someone like you could

337
00:18:21,660 --> 00:18:24,697
defeat a great game master
like Maximillian Pegasus?

338
00:18:24,780 --> 00:18:27,757
You can't even hold your own
in Dungeon Dice Monsters!

339
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:29,980
Just listen to me, Devlin! Never!

340
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:34,457
Your hero worship of Pegasus has
completely blinded you to the truth!

341
00:18:34,540 --> 00:18:35,370
No,

342
00:18:35,453 --> 00:18:36,337
I can see perfectly,

343
00:18:36,420 --> 00:18:40,697
and I see a cheater who's about to be
retired from Duel Monsters forever!

344
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:42,140
Now roll, you fraud!

345
00:18:42,660 --> 00:18:45,700
I will roll, and I will defeat you!

346
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:48,750
There!

347
00:18:48,833 --> 00:18:51,020
I rolled two level 3 Summon Crests.

348
00:18:51,180 --> 00:18:52,945
That's another monster for me!

349
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:54,560
Dimension the Dice!

350
00:18:55,020 --> 00:18:57,600
And unlock Thunderball!

351
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:03,030
Thunderball.

352
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:08,137
Thunderball may be a third level monster,
but his stats really aren't that strong.

353
00:19:08,220 --> 00:19:11,338
I'm afraid he's not going
to be a lot of help to you.

354
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:14,717
Unless, that is, Yugi uses
Thunderball's special attack.

355
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:16,920
Too bad he doesn't know how.

356
00:19:17,460 --> 00:19:18,740
My turn now.

357
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:20,800
Go! Dice roll!

358
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:23,190
Yes!

359
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:25,600
One attack and two movement crests.

360
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:29,940
I'll advance my blast lizard and
gator dragon into attack position.

361
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:32,220
Look out, Yugi!

362
00:19:32,440 --> 00:19:34,852
That gator dragon's finally reached Yugi!

363
00:19:34,940 --> 00:19:36,017
Yugi's heart points.

364
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:37,260
They're in range.

365
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:40,120
That's right, Yugi.

366
00:19:40,320 --> 00:19:43,420
My gator dragon is poised
to take your heart.

367
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:50,580
And now, Gator Dragon, attack
him with Swamp Fire Blast!

368
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:56,600
Oh, no!

369
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:59,760
He wiped out Yugi's heart
point just like that!

370
00:20:00,360 --> 00:20:01,480
We love Duke!

371
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:02,980
He's so cute!

372
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:04,837
When he smiles, he...

373
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:06,900
Would y 'all shut up?

374
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:08,981
My friend's in real trouble here!

375
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:10,737
Ah, we're a giant trouble!

376
00:20:10,820 --> 00:20:11,757
Someone help me!

377
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:13,180
Ha ha ha ha!

378
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:15,777
Now you only have two heart points, Yu-Gi!

379
00:20:15,860 --> 00:20:16,980
But not for long,

380
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:19,077
because my monsters are already lined up

381
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:21,477
and ready to take them
out in the next round.

382
00:20:21,560 --> 00:20:22,480
This is bad.

383
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:25,960
The whole world's about
to see you lose, Yu-Gi!

384
00:20:26,280 --> 00:20:29,809
Then you'll be forced to retire
from dual monsters in shame!

385
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:34,860
Pegasus will be avenged, and you'll
be exposed as the sham that you are!

386
00:20:35,380 --> 00:20:36,257
Ha ha ha ha!

387
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:38,197
Come on, Yu-Gi! Ha ha ha!

388
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:39,237
What can I do?

389
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:43,617
Duke's got more monsters, more dungeon
path and more heart points than me.

390
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:45,994
And he's in a position to attack again.

391
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:48,300
How can I possibly win?

392
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:50,618
How can I beat Duke at his own game?
